#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=9 nAlgorithms=6;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree App (version 6.7.8, built 20 May 2026)';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1779616896164'; [Sun May 24 12:01:36 CEST 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using SplitsTree App 6.0.0 (Huson and Bryant 2024).
The original input consisted of 7 taxa and 7 DNAwithAmbiguityCodes sequences of length 5,454.
After removal of one taxon, the input consisted of 6 taxa and 6 DNAwithAmbiguityCodes sequences of length 5,454.
The P Distance method (Hamming 1950) was used (default options) so as to obtain a 6 x 6 distance matrix.
The Neighbor Net method (Bryant & Moulton 2004, Bryant & Huson 2023) was used (default options) so as to obtain 13 splits, circular.
The Show Splits method was used (default options) so as to obtain a Split Network visualization.

References:
Bryant & Huson 2023: D. Bryant and DH Huson, NeighborNet- improved algorithms and implementation. Front. Bioinform. 3, 2023.
Bryant & Moulton 2004: D. Bryant and V. Moulton. Neighbor-net: An agglomerative method for the construction of phylogenetic networks. Molecular Biology and Evolution, 21(2):255– 265, 2004.
Hamming 1950: Hamming, Richard W. Error detecting and error correcting codes. Bell System Technical Journal. 29 (2): 147–160. MR 0035935, 1950.
Huson and Bryant 2024: D.H. Huson and D. Bryant. The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods, 2024.
]

BEGIN TAXA;
TITLE 'Input Taxa';
LINK ALGORITHM = 'Input Data Loader';
DIMENSIONS ntax=7;
TAXLABELS
	[1] 'An_arabiensis'
	[2] 'An_coluzzii'
	[3] 'An_quadriannulatus'
	[4] 'An_merus'
	[5] 'An_gambiae'
	[6] 'An_christyi'
	[7] 'An_melas'
;
